1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
== Official Website www.kissasia.co  ==

2
00:00:00,259 --> 00:00:01,259
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:01,259 --> 00:00:02,259
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:02,259 --> 00:00:03,992
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:56,226 --> 00:00:59,359
[Episode 5]

6
00:01:03,451 --> 00:01:06,011
Honey, what are you doing?

7
00:01:06,011 --> 00:01:07,927
Oh? You're already up?

8
00:01:07,927 --> 00:01:09,592
Why don't you sleep a little longer?

9
00:01:09,592 --> 00:01:12,243
What is it? Are you making breakfast?

10
00:01:12,243 --> 00:01:14,059
No, sit down first.

11
00:01:14,059 --> 00:01:15,283
Huh?

12
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:18,823
I woke up early for once,
so I thought I'd show off my skills.

13
00:01:18,823 --> 00:01:20,792
Wow, really?

14
00:01:23,799 --> 00:01:29,426
This boiled egg is just like you,
honest, plain, and exactly as it is.

15
00:01:29,426 --> 00:01:33,575
This good-looking fried egg
is just like me, rich and savory,

16
00:01:33,575 --> 00:01:35,492
with a drizzle of sesame oil.

17
00:01:38,015 --> 00:01:40,163
These scrambled eggs are tiny and cute,

18
00:01:40,163 --> 00:01:43,391
loaded with butter and milk,
just like our Yul.

19
00:01:43,391 --> 00:01:46,079
It's all eggs, isn't it?

20
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:47,826
No, it's not.

21
00:01:49,535 --> 00:01:50,547
Ta-da!

22
00:01:50,547 --> 00:01:52,875
This colorful salad and sandwich,

23
00:01:52,875 --> 00:01:56,139
with all three of our
unique personalities together.

24
00:01:56,139 --> 00:01:58,827
Wow, my husband is the best, huh?

25
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:01,055
When did you make all this by yourself?

26
00:02:01,055 --> 00:02:03,507
Your mom would faint if she found out.

27
00:02:03,507 --> 00:02:06,355
Gosh, she can never find out.

28
00:02:06,355 --> 00:02:10,526
How am I supposed to
weather the storm if she does?

29
00:02:11,919 --> 00:02:14,626
You seem to be in a really
good mood today, honey.

30
00:02:14,626 --> 00:02:15,626
Of course, I am.

31
00:02:15,626 --> 00:02:20,575
I have the two most precious treasures
in the world right here beside me.

32
00:02:20,575 --> 00:02:22,535
And speaking of that...

33
00:02:22,535 --> 00:02:24,063
Mommy!

34
00:02:24,063 --> 00:02:25,279
Yul, are you up?

35
00:02:25,279 --> 00:02:26,727
Is my baby girl awake?

36
00:02:26,727 --> 00:02:28,659
Did you sleep well?

37
00:02:29,703 --> 00:02:32,387
Daddy made all this breakfast
for you and Mommy. See?

38
00:02:32,387 --> 00:02:35,659
- Let's eat quickly.
- Yay! I'll dig in with Kkongsoon.

39
00:02:35,659 --> 00:02:37,359
Okay.

40
00:02:41,383 --> 00:02:43,192
Kkongsoon?

41
00:02:44,795 --> 00:02:48,526
When did we get a new member
of the family without me knowing?

42
00:02:51,115 --> 00:02:53,055
Yul! Look at this!

43
00:02:53,055 --> 00:02:55,817
Your mommy's friend
sent you a doll as a gift.

44
00:02:55,817 --> 00:02:57,059
Mommy, give it to me.

45
00:02:57,059 --> 00:02:58,792
Here.

46
00:03:00,287 --> 00:03:01,843
Oh, I'm jealous.

47
00:03:01,843 --> 00:03:04,926
You have a friend who even
sends you gifts from overseas.

48
00:03:04,926 --> 00:03:07,059
Indeed, having good friends is nice.

49
00:03:07,059 --> 00:03:09,703
Oh, that Russian friend you're close to?

50
00:03:09,703 --> 00:03:11,626
Is the name Seul Gi?

51
00:03:11,626 --> 00:03:12,895
Yeah, that's right, Seul Gi.

52
00:03:12,895 --> 00:03:14,675
Come to think of it,
I've never even seen this friend's face.

53
00:03:14,675 --> 00:03:17,192
Seul Gi couldn't come to
our wedding either, right?

54
00:03:17,192 --> 00:03:19,919
I'll introduce you
when Seul Gi comes to Korea.

55
00:03:19,919 --> 00:03:22,319
Anyway, I'm grateful to that friend.

56
00:03:22,319 --> 00:03:24,629
Please send Seul Gi my thanks, double for me.

57
00:03:24,629 --> 00:03:26,692
I already did right after I got it.

58
00:03:31,803 --> 00:03:33,959
How's the weather over there these days?

59
00:03:33,959 --> 00:03:36,603
Does it rain on and off?

60
00:03:36,603 --> 00:03:37,983
How are you holding up?

61
00:03:37,983 --> 00:03:41,127
You've always hated rain
ever since you were little.

62
00:03:41,127 --> 00:03:43,759
You used to be scared
of thunder and lightning.

63
00:03:53,583 --> 00:03:59,526
If you do this one more time,
I'll deep-fry you with a lightning bolt.

64
00:04:06,227 --> 00:04:08,292
Yul, you shouldn't do that.

65
00:04:08,292 --> 00:04:09,459
Yul, you need to eat this.

66
00:04:09,459 --> 00:04:10,626
No, you can't.

67
00:04:10,626 --> 00:04:14,075
Yul, you have to eat!

68
00:04:14,075 --> 00:04:15,599
You need to eat your food.

69
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:17,992
I'm going to catch you, Yul!

70
00:04:22,035 --> 00:04:24,559
[Not Today]

71
00:04:37,199 --> 00:04:38,526
[Caller ID Restricted:
You keep your promises well]

72
00:04:38,526 --> 00:04:40,226
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong]

73
00:04:46,851 --> 00:04:49,911
Given that Pyo Kyu Cheol
was also killed by a sniper,

74
00:04:49,911 --> 00:04:51,792
should we conclude that the previous
Jeonjak-dong Hotel incident

75
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:54,839
- was also the work of Kingfisher?
- Oh, my, I knew it was too quiet.

76
00:04:54,839 --> 00:04:56,892
[Can Kingfisher's Return Be Confirmed?]
Of course. Otherwise, how could

77
00:04:56,892 --> 00:04:59,351
- a string of gun murders happen
- You're here?

78
00:04:59,351 --> 00:05:01,326
- in South Korea?
- It was quiet for a few days.

79
00:05:01,326 --> 00:05:04,255
- So, the return of Kingfisher is confirmed.
- And now it's dominating the headlines.

80
00:05:04,255 --> 00:05:08,326
At times like this,
whatever article I write gets buried.

81
00:05:08,963 --> 00:05:10,947
Whatever I say gets drowned out.

82
00:05:10,947 --> 00:05:15,199
He doesn't even listen to me.
Whatever I say gets buried.

83
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:16,775
Hey, wait up!

84
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:21,363
Hey, I heard someone fell
to their death at a construction site.

85
00:05:21,363 --> 00:05:23,892
Oh, my. How did that happen?

86
00:05:23,892 --> 00:05:27,275
The chief wants me to
look into what happened.

87
00:05:27,275 --> 00:05:28,759
Apparently, someone sent in a tip.

88
00:05:28,759 --> 00:05:32,303
"It was an unjust death, reveal the truth,"
and all that nonsense.

89
00:05:32,303 --> 00:05:34,292
Really?

90
00:05:35,431 --> 00:05:39,727
Then dig deep. Fighting.

91
00:05:39,727 --> 00:05:41,259
Here's what I think.

92
00:05:41,259 --> 00:05:42,559
I'd bet this was 100%

93
00:05:42,559 --> 00:05:45,211
an unfortunate accident
caused by safety violations.

94
00:05:45,211 --> 00:05:47,935
If the media starts stirring things up
and digging around,

95
00:05:47,935 --> 00:05:51,007
we could end up bringing down
a perfectly good company

96
00:05:51,007 --> 00:05:53,199
and even causing unexpected ripple effects
on our economy, don't you think?

97
00:05:53,199 --> 00:05:55,823
I wish my colleague Go Ji Soon
would stop talking nonsense

98
00:05:55,823 --> 00:05:59,792
and be faithful to a reporter's
sense of mission and the press's duty.

99
00:05:59,792 --> 00:06:01,459
Well, I have another thought.

100
00:06:01,459 --> 00:06:03,681
If my colleague, Mr. Kwon,

101
00:06:03,681 --> 00:06:06,831
who is always devoted to
his mission and duty as a reporter,

102
00:06:06,831 --> 00:06:09,807
were to investigate this case in my place,

103
00:06:09,807 --> 00:06:14,326
maybe he could "dig into it
much more thoroughly," right?

104
00:06:16,159 --> 00:06:18,159
That's a good idea, huh?

105
00:06:19,592 --> 00:06:20,999
Good idea...

106
00:06:20,999 --> 00:06:22,699
Hey, seriously?

107
00:06:24,163 --> 00:06:27,459
[Seoul Nambu Police Station]
What? A joint investigation?

108
00:06:30,099 --> 00:06:32,167
Whose bright idea was this?

109
00:06:32,167 --> 00:06:34,719
We've reached a preliminary agreement
with the station handling the case.

110
00:06:34,719 --> 00:06:37,126
If you just approve it, Chief...

111
00:06:38,263 --> 00:06:40,031
I told you not to stir things up.

112
00:06:40,031 --> 00:06:44,195
The Pyo Kyu Cheol case is different
from Kingfisher's usual methods.

113
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:46,159
If we cooperate,
we might be able to find a lead...

114
00:06:46,159 --> 00:06:50,359
I don't see why you need to do this.

115
00:06:50,359 --> 00:06:54,975
That punk's case is finally off my hands.
My 10-year ulcer is healing.

116
00:06:54,975 --> 00:06:57,855
Everyone else is desperate
to get that burden off their hands.

117
00:06:57,855 --> 00:07:00,692
What makes you so special?

118
00:07:01,631 --> 00:07:08,235
Are you aiming for a few ranks'
worth of promotions or something?

119
00:07:08,235 --> 00:07:09,603
That's not it.

120
00:07:09,603 --> 00:07:11,423
Then back off.

121
00:07:11,423 --> 00:07:14,223
You know our precinct's performance
is at the bottom this quarter, right?

122
00:07:14,223 --> 00:07:17,219
Instead of worrying about
another precinct's case,

123
00:07:17,219 --> 00:07:20,007
you should nab a few more
petty crooks in our own precinct...

124
00:07:20,007 --> 00:07:21,871
Even one...

125
00:07:21,871 --> 00:07:22,879
Huh?

126
00:07:22,879 --> 00:07:24,579
Wait...

127
00:07:25,387 --> 00:07:27,999
That punk's ignoring me while I'm talking.

128
00:07:27,999 --> 00:07:30,063
I told you to back off, okay?

129
00:07:30,063 --> 00:07:32,123
Beom!

130
00:07:32,123 --> 00:07:37,091
He could say, "Hey, you're that fired up?
Want to suffer a bit more?"

131
00:07:37,091 --> 00:07:39,491
He knows I'll just suffer with no results.

132
00:07:39,491 --> 00:07:42,019
We're not even asking for more personnel.

133
00:07:42,019 --> 00:07:44,859
The Chief is just doing his job.

134
00:07:48,683 --> 00:07:51,427
Why didn't you mention the accidental deaths
of those child sex offenders?

135
00:07:51,427 --> 00:07:53,755
There's no solid evidence.
It's all speculation.

136
00:07:53,755 --> 00:07:57,927
You said you weren't sure if we'd been
barking up the wrong tree or not.

137
00:07:57,927 --> 00:08:01,939
If we're wrong, the eight prior
accidental deaths were all coincidences.

138
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:05,155
I still can't make sense of it,
even after thinking it over all night.

139
00:08:05,155 --> 00:08:06,392
But if we were right?

140
00:08:06,392 --> 00:08:09,371
Then all the prior deaths were accidents,
and this one was a shooting.

141
00:08:09,371 --> 00:08:10,591
Why on earth?

142
00:08:10,591 --> 00:08:12,171
Why only this time?

143
00:08:12,171 --> 00:08:14,527
Maybe they planned for it to look like
an accident, but something went wrong,

144
00:08:14,527 --> 00:08:17,031
and they had to finish the job with a sniper.

145
00:08:17,031 --> 00:08:20,559
Wow, if that's the case...

146
00:08:20,559 --> 00:08:26,026
Sniping isn't the only method
Kingfisher uses.

147
00:08:26,026 --> 00:08:29,126
Wow, this is getting big.

148
00:08:29,792 --> 00:08:31,026
What are you going to do now?

149
00:08:31,026 --> 00:08:33,626
The chief is making a huge fuss
about telling us to back off, isn't he?

150
00:08:40,543 --> 00:08:42,799
You're here?

151
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:45,359
That guy sent a gift from Russia.

152
00:08:50,075 --> 00:08:52,215
That guy's sticky fingers are still the same.

153
00:08:52,215 --> 00:08:54,326
Russian-made stuff is pretty useful.

154
00:08:57,047 --> 00:08:59,079
Let's see if there's
anything worth salvaging.

155
00:08:59,079 --> 00:09:00,889
Looks like that guy's gotten restless again.

156
00:09:00,889 --> 00:09:03,159
I heard that the guy
will be coming to Korea soon.

157
00:09:03,159 --> 00:09:06,111
Gosh, I hate seeing that face.

158
00:09:06,111 --> 00:09:10,627
Yeah? Then I'll have to make sure you don't.

159
00:09:10,627 --> 00:09:14,343
Wow, this thing is still alive? Huh?

160
00:09:14,343 --> 00:09:17,775
I thought it'd suffocate
and die within a few days.

161
00:09:17,775 --> 00:09:20,487
Did you give it some water?

162
00:09:20,487 --> 00:09:23,426
It couldn't have been you taking care of it.

163
00:09:24,087 --> 00:09:26,159
Whoever it was, I'm grateful.

164
00:09:28,803 --> 00:09:32,355
I guess you're alive thanks to this guy, huh?

165
00:09:32,355 --> 00:09:34,787
You've worked hard for three years,
air-purifying plant.

166
00:09:34,787 --> 00:09:36,126
It's Tae Soon.

167
00:09:36,126 --> 00:09:38,592
It's even fresh and lively.

168
00:09:40,539 --> 00:09:44,599
You really have no concept of time,
now or then...

169
00:09:44,599 --> 00:09:47,926
It's April, you know. April.

170
00:09:49,371 --> 00:09:53,015
Being trapped in here like this,
I guess even I would lose track of time...

171
00:09:53,015 --> 00:09:54,892
April...

172
00:09:56,687 --> 00:09:58,515
April...

173
00:09:58,515 --> 00:09:59,835
[Client Meeting Pre-Briefing]

174
00:09:59,835 --> 00:10:01,855
His name is Tak Jong Gu.

175
00:10:01,855 --> 00:10:05,855
His dad is a five-term congressman,
and his mom is a chaebol heiress.

176
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:08,726
He's the notorious youngest son
of the so-called Royal Family.

177
00:10:08,726 --> 00:10:10,235
[Client Information: Personal Details]

178
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:11,379
Let's have something good to drink.

179
00:10:11,379 --> 00:10:13,079
Something fun.

180
00:10:13,979 --> 00:10:17,519
He drugged women, sexually assaulted them,

181
00:10:17,519 --> 00:10:20,271
and even filmed and distributed the footage.

182
00:10:20,271 --> 00:10:23,823
Dozens of videos were found on his computer,

183
00:10:23,823 --> 00:10:27,626
yet he got off with
just a two-year suspended sentence.

184
00:10:28,407 --> 00:10:29,859
A suspended sentence?

185
00:10:29,859 --> 00:10:34,559
He had lawyers from a major law firm
settle with the victims one by one.

186
00:10:34,559 --> 00:10:37,987
Settlement is one way to put it.
It was probably money and threats.

187
00:10:37,987 --> 00:10:39,799
Right now, he's holed up
at the Hongseon casino,

188
00:10:39,799 --> 00:10:42,479
gambling away merrily.

189
00:10:42,479 --> 00:10:44,975
So the Gold class is the type with
a lot of money and connections, huh?

190
00:10:44,975 --> 00:10:46,707
The kind who can wriggle out of anything
despite their crimes.

191
00:10:46,707 --> 00:10:49,026
They're the biggest headache.

192
00:10:49,679 --> 00:10:52,392
They're usually heavily guarded,
so getting close to them isn't easy.

193
00:10:52,392 --> 00:10:54,251
And it doesn't come cheap, either.

194
00:10:54,251 --> 00:10:56,495
Especially when we're barely
keeping our operating expenses afloat.

195
00:10:56,495 --> 00:10:58,235
- A casino?
- Yeah.

196
00:10:58,235 --> 00:11:02,995
His dad is aiming to become
National Assembly Speaker in a month.

197
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:05,411
So he was given strict orders to lie low

198
00:11:05,411 --> 00:11:08,647
somewhere out of the public eye until then.

199
00:11:08,647 --> 00:11:11,411
Tak Jong Gu is easily excitable
and has weak self-control.

200
00:11:11,411 --> 00:11:14,731
So he's susceptible to gambling addiction.

201
00:11:14,731 --> 00:11:16,743
[Client Information: Criminal History]
He has no sense of guilt, either.

202
00:11:16,743 --> 00:11:18,887
Five years ago, a woman in her twenties

203
00:11:18,887 --> 00:11:21,426
fell to her death from a high-rise apartment.

204
00:11:21,426 --> 00:11:24,459
Tak Jong Gu was there too.

205
00:11:25,071 --> 00:11:26,611
Darn it.

206
00:11:26,611 --> 00:11:28,359
Why were you acting up?

207
00:11:28,359 --> 00:11:30,726
How did he get away with it back then?

208
00:11:32,647 --> 00:11:37,231
He claimed they had a fight and that
she impulsively jumped to her death.

209
00:11:37,231 --> 00:11:42,026
The court acquitted him
due to insufficient evidence.

210
00:11:44,335 --> 00:11:46,547
This one's quite an upgrade, huh?

211
00:11:46,547 --> 00:11:48,092
Seems like the world's
getting easier to push around.

212
00:11:48,092 --> 00:11:50,259
[Tak Jong Gu's social media post:
The world is on my side again]

213
00:11:50,259 --> 00:11:51,259
[Law can go to the dogs]

214
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:55,599
Alright, he's holed up in the provinces.

215
00:11:55,599 --> 00:11:58,171
We'll have to go on a business trip.

216
00:11:58,171 --> 00:12:01,226
These days, faking an accidental death

217
00:12:01,226 --> 00:12:04,007
with some half-baked scenario
just won't cut it.

218
00:12:04,007 --> 00:12:07,375
We're living in the age of
cutting-edge forensics.

219
00:12:07,375 --> 00:12:11,927
Oh, coming up with a scenario
for every meeting is the hardest part.

220
00:12:11,927 --> 00:12:17,159
Figuring out how to kill someone is
harder than figuring out how to save them.

221
00:12:19,619 --> 00:12:21,559
I'll handle this one.

222
00:12:22,487 --> 00:12:24,187
You will, Director Yoo?

223
00:12:25,459 --> 00:12:29,767
But considering the unexpected
Pyo Kyu Cheol incident

224
00:12:29,767 --> 00:12:32,431
stirred up the media and police,

225
00:12:32,431 --> 00:12:36,192
wouldn't it be risky to do
another one right away?

226
00:12:39,411 --> 00:12:43,147
If we're doing it, I hope we hit the jackpot
on the meeting day.

227
00:12:43,147 --> 00:12:47,992
Make the day of greatest joy
become his ancestral rite day, right?

228
00:12:53,019 --> 00:12:54,719
Ancestral rite...

229
00:12:57,303 --> 00:12:59,026
What day is it today?

230
00:13:01,051 --> 00:13:04,026
[Mother]

231
00:13:08,203 --> 00:13:10,759
Hello, Mother.

232
00:13:12,535 --> 00:13:15,295
Of course, I know.

233
00:13:15,295 --> 00:13:16,995
Yeah.

234
00:13:24,243 --> 00:13:25,763
Assistant Manager Yang,
I still have my half-day off, right?

235
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:29,392
Please. We'll continue
the meeting tomorrow. Sorry.

236
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:37,903
Director Yoo must attend
the ancestral rite at her in-laws' house.

237
00:13:37,903 --> 00:13:39,259
Of course, she does.
She's the daughter-in-law.

238
00:13:39,259 --> 00:13:41,691
So Kingfisher has become
a daughter-in-law now too.

239
00:13:41,691 --> 00:13:43,451
On a day like this, isn't she less
a daughter-in-law and more a servant?

240
00:13:43,451 --> 00:13:45,626
I should probably come with her...

241
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:05,892
I think this is the place.

242
00:14:05,892 --> 00:14:11,526
[My Safety, My Coworkers' Safety]

243
00:14:16,247 --> 00:14:18,293
Two weeks ago, a worker fell to his death

244
00:14:18,293 --> 00:14:20,467
while organizing materials
on the sixth floor.

245
00:14:20,467 --> 00:14:22,475
The investigation concluded
that it was an accident

246
00:14:22,475 --> 00:14:25,800
caused by his own negligence, correct?

247
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:28,159
That's what's been made public.

248
00:14:28,159 --> 00:14:29,355
Now we need to find out for ourselves.

249
00:14:29,355 --> 00:14:34,892
Whether it was just an accident
or an unjust death disguised as one.

250
00:14:34,892 --> 00:14:37,315
While everyone's
focused on the Kingfisher case,

251
00:14:37,315 --> 00:14:38,743
we'll investigate the unjust death of

252
00:14:38,743 --> 00:14:42,592
the socially vulnerable
left in the blind spot?

253
00:14:43,992 --> 00:14:45,911
I really like this kind of stuff.

254
00:14:45,911 --> 00:14:48,759
This is what being a reporter is all about.

255
00:14:48,759 --> 00:14:50,492
Let's go, Mr. Kwon.

256
00:14:57,503 --> 00:14:59,991
I mean, the police already came and went.

257
00:14:59,991 --> 00:15:03,631
The Ministry of Employment and Labor
and the Ministry of Land investigated too.

258
00:15:03,631 --> 00:15:07,379
It was all determined
to be personal negligence.

259
00:15:07,379 --> 00:15:11,995
Really? Then what were the names
of the officials who came out that day?

260
00:15:11,995 --> 00:15:14,426
Well, still, our chairman said

261
00:15:14,426 --> 00:15:17,723
the company had a moral obligation,
so we covered workers' compensation,

262
00:15:17,723 --> 00:15:22,292
the death benefit, and even added
a hefty condolence payment.

263
00:15:22,292 --> 00:15:28,091
There's no one as generous as our chairman.

264
00:15:28,091 --> 00:15:29,499
I see.

265
00:15:29,499 --> 00:15:33,692
I'll ask the chairman about that myself.
Where can I meet him?

266
00:15:34,343 --> 00:15:38,903
Well, it's rather difficult
to meet the chairman in person.

267
00:15:38,903 --> 00:15:43,235
Then what about the coworkers who worked
with the deceased, Kang Yeong Ho?

268
00:15:43,235 --> 00:15:45,355
Oh, that's possible.

269
00:15:45,355 --> 00:15:46,795
Oh, there's one right over there.

270
00:15:46,795 --> 00:15:49,426
- Mr. Park Chun Bok!
- Yes.

271
00:15:50,363 --> 00:15:52,959
Go talk to him.

272
00:15:57,743 --> 00:16:01,411
That fellow Kang Yeong Ho,
he reeked of alcohol that day.

273
00:16:01,411 --> 00:16:06,055
I don't know if he'd been drinking
all morning or was still hungover.

274
00:16:06,055 --> 00:16:08,314
It had happened a few times before too.

275
00:16:08,314 --> 00:16:12,026
That day too, he didn't wear his hard hat,
so I warned him several times.

276
00:16:12,026 --> 00:16:13,867
Yeah.

277
00:16:13,867 --> 00:16:15,191
I see.

278
00:16:15,191 --> 00:16:19,086
Did you report that to the company as well?

279
00:16:19,086 --> 00:16:23,626
Do you think I feel good talking about
a former colleague like that?

280
00:16:23,626 --> 00:16:25,611
Besides, he's dead.

281
00:16:25,611 --> 00:16:28,807
Still, I thought I should be honest
about what happened.

282
00:16:28,807 --> 00:16:31,847
- Yeah.
- Of course, you should have.

283
00:16:31,847 --> 00:16:35,943
Even after all that, the chairman
was incredibly generous, wasn't he?

284
00:16:35,943 --> 00:16:37,249
Yeah.

285
00:16:37,249 --> 00:16:40,259
So everyone seems pretty grateful
to the chairman.

286
00:16:40,259 --> 00:16:42,703
We were at a loss
because the construction was delayed too.

287
00:16:42,703 --> 00:16:47,092
The chairman even made sure
we got our wages in advance.

288
00:16:54,063 --> 00:16:56,247
I mean, the company
processed the industrial accident,

289
00:16:56,247 --> 00:16:58,971
paid the compensation,
and even gave a condolence payment.

290
00:16:58,971 --> 00:17:01,899
Didn't they do everything
they were supposed to?

291
00:17:01,899 --> 00:17:05,147
That's not something companies usually do.

292
00:17:05,147 --> 00:17:06,961
You know it well.

293
00:17:06,961 --> 00:17:08,059
Pardon?

294
00:17:08,059 --> 00:17:12,147
He smelled of alcohol
and wasn't wearing a hard hat.

295
00:17:12,147 --> 00:17:13,387
In such cases, companies usually

296
00:17:13,387 --> 00:17:15,859
highlight personal negligence
and cut ties without mercy.

297
00:17:15,859 --> 00:17:17,892
That's how companies operate.

298
00:17:18,551 --> 00:17:23,059
But the chairman stepped in
and went all out with compensation?

299
00:17:23,059 --> 00:17:28,035
And this so-called witness
just happens to show up

300
00:17:28,035 --> 00:17:30,703
and start talking about
the victim's negligence.

301
00:17:30,703 --> 00:17:33,219
Oh, you're right.

302
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:34,827
So what do we do now?

303
00:17:34,827 --> 00:17:36,767
We don't even know
who the informant is, do we?

304
00:17:36,767 --> 00:17:38,467
Well, that's...

305
00:17:40,292 --> 00:17:42,475
[Receive Gaecheon Construction
Meal Tickets Here]

306
00:17:42,475 --> 00:17:45,359
Let's grab some food first
and look into it afterward.

307
00:17:45,359 --> 00:17:48,492
We're eating again?
We just ate before we came.

308
00:17:52,351 --> 00:17:54,767
- Take a look before you go.
- I'll be right back.

309
00:17:54,767 --> 00:17:57,443
- Yeah.
- It's been a while.

310
00:17:57,443 --> 00:17:59,147
You know we're not serving
steamed rice cake, right?

311
00:17:59,147 --> 00:18:01,849
- You're here?
- Oh, really? Hello.

312
00:18:01,849 --> 00:18:03,711
Hey, I'm here.

313
00:18:03,711 --> 00:18:05,459
Oh, Tae Seong's family is here.

314
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:06,592
The baby's mom came too?

315
00:18:06,592 --> 00:18:08,007
Yeah, have you been well?

316
00:18:08,007 --> 00:18:09,111
Welcome.

317
00:18:09,111 --> 00:18:13,759
Seeing you bring your daughter-in-law,
it must be an ancestral rite day.

318
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:17,131
Don't make that delicate daughter-in-law
do all the work every time.

319
00:18:17,131 --> 00:18:18,795
Bring that precious son of yours too.

320
00:18:18,795 --> 00:18:21,417
Oh, please. Why would my son come here?

321
00:18:21,417 --> 00:18:23,634
He's busy working at the company.

322
00:18:23,634 --> 00:18:27,115
Anyway, you're always going on
about your son, all year round.

323
00:18:27,115 --> 00:18:30,203
So, what kind of fish are you making?

324
00:18:30,203 --> 00:18:34,183
- Hey, you pick one out.
- What?

325
00:18:34,183 --> 00:18:37,692
Pick out what you think we should buy.

326
00:18:38,999 --> 00:18:41,692
Oh, okay.

327
00:18:46,587 --> 00:18:47,599
How about this, Mother?

328
00:18:47,599 --> 00:18:48,823
Oh, my.

329
00:18:48,823 --> 00:18:50,833
- Oh, what am I going to do?
- It's so shiny.

330
00:18:50,833 --> 00:18:52,791
Oh, jeez.

331
00:18:52,791 --> 00:18:56,626
Hey, I told you clearly that fish
whose names end in "chi" are low-grade

332
00:18:56,626 --> 00:19:00,428
and shouldn't go on
the memorial table, didn't I?

333
00:19:00,428 --> 00:19:03,513
How can you keep doing this
when I've told you so many times?

334
00:19:03,513 --> 00:19:05,951
Oh, jeez.

335
00:19:05,951 --> 00:19:08,392
She never told me that.

336
00:19:10,631 --> 00:19:14,426
I'm sorry, Mother. I'll make sure
to remember from now on.

337
00:19:14,426 --> 00:19:19,526
Then, among the ones
that don't end in "chi"...

338
00:19:20,525 --> 00:19:21,819
This is a croaker, right?

339
00:19:21,819 --> 00:19:23,843
Yeah, croaker!

340
00:19:23,843 --> 00:19:26,226
This one's saury?

341
00:19:27,187 --> 00:19:28,875
And that one is mackerel?

342
00:19:28,875 --> 00:19:30,307
And this one's pomfret!

343
00:19:30,307 --> 00:19:31,859
Am I right, Mother?

344
00:19:31,859 --> 00:19:35,726
Oh, my, now you know it perfectly
without even being told?

345
00:19:35,726 --> 00:19:38,963
So, we can't have saury and mackerel,
which end in "chi,"

346
00:19:38,963 --> 00:19:42,559
so please give me pomfret and croaker,
which don't end in "chi."

347
00:19:42,559 --> 00:19:43,663
Oh, okay.

348
00:19:43,663 --> 00:19:45,926
- And some abalone too.
- Okay.

349
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:56,827
Kang Yeong Ho? He was drinking?

350
00:19:56,827 --> 00:19:59,579
Oh, my, where did you hear such nonsense?

351
00:19:59,579 --> 00:20:03,314
Right? See? I told you it wasn't true.

352
00:20:03,314 --> 00:20:06,163
- Pardon?
- I mean, she kept insisting that

353
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:07,863
everyone at the construction site drinks,

354
00:20:07,863 --> 00:20:12,259
and that Kang Yeong Ho caused the accident
because he was still drunk that day.

355
00:20:14,526 --> 00:20:16,326
Oh, that's right. I remember now.

356
00:20:16,326 --> 00:20:19,575
I had a bit of a preconceived notion.

357
00:20:19,575 --> 00:20:22,559
You shouldn't make someone
so wrongfully accused like that.

358
00:20:22,559 --> 00:20:25,292
That man never even touched alcohol.

359
00:20:25,292 --> 00:20:30,763
Even when he had something really upsetting
going on, I never saw him drink.

360
00:20:30,763 --> 00:20:32,027
Something upsetting?

361
00:20:32,027 --> 00:20:36,815
Yeah, I heard something happened to his wife.

362
00:20:36,815 --> 00:20:41,167
That guy absolutely adored his wife.

363
00:20:41,167 --> 00:20:44,251
As they say these days,
he was a total wife guy.

364
00:20:44,251 --> 00:20:48,359
Oh, sounds just like me.

365
00:20:50,743 --> 00:20:56,423
Wait, now that I think about it, his wife
used to work at the chairman's house.

366
00:20:56,423 --> 00:20:59,226
That's enough, right? Enjoy your meal.

367
00:21:02,039 --> 00:21:03,959
The chairman's house?

368
00:21:14,323 --> 00:21:16,175
- Oh, my.
- They're here.

369
00:21:16,175 --> 00:21:18,203
Mommy!

370
00:21:18,203 --> 00:21:19,895
Yul, what were you playing?

371
00:21:19,895 --> 00:21:24,383
I was playing with Auntie,
Kkongsoon, and Chiba.

372
00:21:24,383 --> 00:21:28,382
Oh, my sister-in-law had to
play pack mule again.

373
00:21:28,382 --> 00:21:30,750
- Jeez!
- Quit nagging and just take the bags.

374
00:21:30,750 --> 00:21:34,026
I'm doing it. I'm doing it.

375
00:21:47,919 --> 00:21:49,539
[Three Years Ago]
Hey!

376
00:21:49,539 --> 00:21:52,104
Have you never chopped an onion before?

377
00:21:52,104 --> 00:21:54,626
Why are you using the knife like that?

378
00:21:54,626 --> 00:21:56,429
Are you cutting a cake or something?

379
00:21:56,429 --> 00:21:59,659
I'm just not used to using it
for this kind of thing.

380
00:22:00,526 --> 00:22:03,959
[Two Years Ago]

381
00:22:05,187 --> 00:22:07,195
Wait, why is this here?

382
00:22:07,195 --> 00:22:10,326
Do we have any Southeast Asian ancestors?

383
00:22:10,955 --> 00:22:13,226
I just bought it for you to try.

384
00:22:13,226 --> 00:22:15,423
[One Year Ago]

385
00:22:15,423 --> 00:22:16,776
Hey!

386
00:22:16,776 --> 00:22:19,139
Did you mix grains into the rice?

387
00:22:19,139 --> 00:22:21,839
For the rice we're putting
on the memorial table?

388
00:22:21,839 --> 00:22:23,819
They say it's good for your health...

389
00:22:23,819 --> 00:22:28,426
Wow, jeez. You're driving me crazy. Really.

390
00:22:41,683 --> 00:22:43,731
Okay!

391
00:22:43,731 --> 00:22:45,431
Should I give it a try?

392
00:23:00,683 --> 00:23:04,151
Hey, did you put garlic
in the seasoned vegetables?

393
00:23:04,151 --> 00:23:06,559
Yes, Mother, for a deeper flavor...

394
00:23:07,759 --> 00:23:10,392
Wait... All of that too?

395
00:23:11,983 --> 00:23:14,514
Mother, I put it in all of...

396
00:23:14,514 --> 00:23:16,019
I'm sorry, Mother. Oh, no.

397
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:19,214
Oh, I'll go right now and buy them again.

398
00:23:19,214 --> 00:23:20,619
I'm sorry.

399
00:23:20,619 --> 00:23:23,859
What are we going to do with all this?

400
00:23:24,479 --> 00:23:25,851
I'll be back.

401
00:23:25,851 --> 00:23:27,793
- Wow, seriously...
- Jeez.

402
00:23:27,793 --> 00:23:30,764
Putting garlic
in ancestral rite vegetables...

403
00:23:30,764 --> 00:23:33,202
No matter how clueless she is,
that's too much.

404
00:23:33,202 --> 00:23:36,779
- It's too much, too much.
- Come on. She might not know.

405
00:23:36,779 --> 00:23:38,139
It's no big deal.

406
00:23:38,139 --> 00:23:40,591
It's because she's an orphan.

407
00:23:40,591 --> 00:23:43,591
She never had parents
to teach her these things.

408
00:23:43,591 --> 00:23:46,023
I knew that line was coming.

409
00:23:46,023 --> 00:23:48,523
You really found your opening, Mom.

410
00:23:48,523 --> 00:23:50,626
Be quiet, you girl!

411
00:23:52,592 --> 00:23:57,559
[Kang Yeong Ho]

412
00:24:01,139 --> 00:24:02,539
Tae Seong, when are you coming?

413
00:24:02,539 --> 00:24:04,239
Is anyone home?

414
00:24:10,547 --> 00:24:12,426
Hello?

415
00:24:14,315 --> 00:24:16,291
I guess no one's here.

416
00:24:16,291 --> 00:24:20,035
Do you really think
Kang Yeong Ho's wife is the informant?

417
00:24:20,035 --> 00:24:21,859
What's the matter?

418
00:24:21,859 --> 00:24:24,551
They moved out. No one lives there now.

419
00:24:24,551 --> 00:24:26,279
They moved? When?

420
00:24:26,279 --> 00:24:28,492
I think it was the day
of the husband's funeral.

421
00:24:28,492 --> 00:24:31,547
They seemed to be in a hurry
and called a moving truck that night.

422
00:24:31,547 --> 00:24:34,399
Do you happen to have
the wife's contact information?

423
00:24:34,399 --> 00:24:36,971
No, we're not close enough
to have each other's numbers.

424
00:24:36,971 --> 00:24:39,383
Is there a real estate office nearby?

425
00:24:39,383 --> 00:24:40,559
A real estate office?

426
00:24:40,559 --> 00:24:42,631
Oh, I guess you're here to look at the house.

427
00:24:42,631 --> 00:24:45,855
Go out of this alley
and turn the corner. It's right there.

428
00:24:45,855 --> 00:24:47,692
Okay, thank you.

429
00:24:50,083 --> 00:24:51,439
Why the real estate office?

430
00:24:51,439 --> 00:24:53,859
If she left in such a hurry, she probably
couldn't even get her deposit back.

431
00:24:53,859 --> 00:24:55,226
She'll have to contact them
eventually, right?

432
00:24:55,226 --> 00:24:56,275
What is she talking about?

433
00:24:56,275 --> 00:24:59,175
Bo Na is going through a rough time.
She's become Mom's lackey.

434
00:24:59,175 --> 00:25:01,743
Tae Seong, you didn't forget about
the ancestral rite today, did you?

435
00:25:01,743 --> 00:25:02,867
Oh!

436
00:25:02,867 --> 00:25:04,303
What is it? What's wrong, Mr. Kwon?

437
00:25:04,303 --> 00:25:05,547
What time is it now?

438
00:25:05,547 --> 00:25:06,867
Right now?

439
00:25:06,867 --> 00:25:08,567
Oh!

440
00:25:09,263 --> 00:25:13,726
Oh, my, I can't live
a long life like this. Jeez.

441
00:25:16,259 --> 00:25:17,331
[I'm in Gangwon Province right now,
but I'll get there as soon as I can]

442
00:25:17,331 --> 00:25:19,259
Gangwon Province?

443
00:25:19,259 --> 00:25:22,559
Oh, my, if he leaves now,
when is he supposed to get here?

444
00:25:23,423 --> 00:25:26,292
Auntie, what's an ancestral rite?

445
00:25:27,279 --> 00:25:29,855
Yul, do you want to know
what an ancestral rite is?

446
00:25:29,855 --> 00:25:32,163
An ancestral rite is...

447
00:25:32,163 --> 00:25:34,071
when people who have gone to heaven

448
00:25:34,071 --> 00:25:38,531
come over to our house to eat,
have fun, and then go back.

449
00:25:38,531 --> 00:25:40,583
What is an orphan?

450
00:25:40,583 --> 00:25:42,283
Huh?

451
00:25:44,515 --> 00:25:48,435
Anyway, Mom said that in front of the child.

452
00:25:48,435 --> 00:25:51,611
That's for parents...

453
00:25:51,611 --> 00:25:57,675
Well, it means Yul's mommy's parents
have passed away.

454
00:25:57,675 --> 00:25:59,992
Is Mommy an orphan?

455
00:26:01,735 --> 00:26:05,959
Yes. Her parents went to heaven
a very long time ago.

456
00:26:05,959 --> 00:26:08,526
Then are they coming over for dinner today?

457
00:26:10,039 --> 00:26:15,191
No. The people coming today are someone else.

458
00:26:15,191 --> 00:26:16,191
Why aren't they coming?

459
00:26:16,191 --> 00:26:19,579
Well... Maybe because they weren't invited?

460
00:26:19,579 --> 00:26:20,887
Then when are they coming?

461
00:26:20,887 --> 00:26:23,023
Oh, well...

462
00:26:23,023 --> 00:26:24,723
If you call them?

463
00:26:27,211 --> 00:26:29,839
They'll come if you call them.

464
00:26:29,839 --> 00:26:32,892
Like, "Please come quickly."

465
00:26:38,143 --> 00:26:39,159
Yul's mommy!

466
00:26:39,159 --> 00:26:41,027
[Ok's Flower Shop]

467
00:26:41,027 --> 00:26:44,126
- Oh, my, ma'am!
- What brings you here at this hour?

468
00:26:47,067 --> 00:26:49,455
Do you have a minute right now?

469
00:26:49,455 --> 00:26:51,655
- Me?
- Yeah.

470
00:26:51,655 --> 00:26:52,931
Right now?

471
00:26:52,931 --> 00:26:55,939
Well... I have to go.

472
00:26:55,939 --> 00:26:57,992
What's going on? Why?

473
00:27:05,847 --> 00:27:07,492
- I'm here.
- Daddy!

474
00:27:07,492 --> 00:27:08,951
Yul!

475
00:27:08,951 --> 00:27:11,119
What? You got here sooner than I expected.

476
00:27:11,119 --> 00:27:12,311
Did you speed all the way here?

477
00:27:12,311 --> 00:27:13,959
Where's Bo Na?
She wasn't answering her phone.

478
00:27:13,959 --> 00:27:17,323
She's on the veranda. And as you can see,
she couldn't answer the phone.

479
00:27:17,323 --> 00:27:18,467
Since the afternoon, all day...

480
00:27:18,467 --> 00:27:20,435
So why was she here all day? What about work?

481
00:27:20,435 --> 00:27:22,347
She took a half-day off.
I guess Mom called her.

482
00:27:22,347 --> 00:27:23,551
Mom's resting in the master bedroom.

483
00:27:23,551 --> 00:27:26,875
- Let's go, Yul! Let's go with Auntie.
- Let's go.

484
00:27:26,875 --> 00:27:29,259
Let's go! Want to draw?

485
00:27:32,783 --> 00:27:35,155
- Honey!
- You're here?

486
00:27:35,155 --> 00:27:38,191
You should have told me.
I almost completely forgot.

487
00:27:38,191 --> 00:27:40,192
Sorry. I forgot too.

488
00:27:41,571 --> 00:27:43,371
Oh, my, really, Mom...

489
00:27:43,371 --> 00:27:45,267
Why did she call someone who works
at a company out in the afternoon?

490
00:27:45,267 --> 00:27:47,791
Come on, it's just one day.
Why are you making a fuss?

491
00:27:47,791 --> 00:27:48,931
There's just a little cleanup left.

492
00:27:48,931 --> 00:27:50,447
It's all done. It's all done.

493
00:27:50,447 --> 00:27:51,491
Rest. I'll do it.

494
00:27:51,491 --> 00:27:53,671
No, don't say things like that.
Just sit over there.

495
00:27:53,671 --> 00:27:56,259
I can finish it quickly before Mom comes out.

496
00:27:59,783 --> 00:28:01,679
- Huh?
- Did you get hurt?

497
00:28:01,679 --> 00:28:06,371
Yeah, I scratched myself while cleaning
the abalone earlier. It was bleeding...

498
00:28:06,371 --> 00:28:07,891
Stay right there.

499
00:28:07,891 --> 00:28:10,559
I put some medicine on it. Honey, it's okay.

500
00:28:13,683 --> 00:28:15,463
I'm okay.

501
00:28:15,463 --> 00:28:17,326
I'm not okay.

502
00:28:20,303 --> 00:28:22,126
It must hurt.

503
00:28:39,227 --> 00:28:41,435
There, done.

504
00:28:41,435 --> 00:28:43,053
It clings just like skin.

505
00:28:43,053 --> 00:28:46,419
You put it on so well
that it's like it's not even there.

506
00:28:46,419 --> 00:28:48,799
And it's easy to move around with.

507
00:28:48,799 --> 00:28:50,147
Thanks.

508
00:28:50,147 --> 00:28:51,199
I should get back to work.

509
00:28:51,199 --> 00:28:52,559
Oh, I told you, it's fine.

510
00:28:52,559 --> 00:28:54,259
Why?

511
00:28:55,175 --> 00:28:56,247
No.

512
00:28:56,247 --> 00:28:57,807
I can just quickly finish
before Mom comes out.

513
00:28:57,807 --> 00:29:00,507
- I'll get in trouble.
- It's okay.

514
00:29:00,507 --> 00:29:03,259
No, she's scary.

515
00:29:10,159 --> 00:29:12,159
Please get some rest.

516
00:29:24,571 --> 00:29:26,271
Mother!

517
00:29:35,311 --> 00:29:36,959
Let's go. Let's go.

518
00:29:36,959 --> 00:29:37,959
It's Yul!

519
00:29:37,959 --> 00:29:39,999
- Yul!
- Auntie!

520
00:29:39,999 --> 00:29:42,047
- When did you get here?
- Have you been well?

521
00:29:42,047 --> 00:29:43,579
How did you two get here together?

522
00:29:43,579 --> 00:29:45,451
Du Ri stopped by the shop and gave me a ride.

523
00:29:45,451 --> 00:29:47,263
What about you? Where are you taking Yul?

524
00:29:47,263 --> 00:29:50,792
Oh, we're going for a walk to the playground.

525
00:29:50,792 --> 00:29:52,126
Really? Oh, my, that sounds nice.

526
00:29:52,126 --> 00:29:53,690
Go on ahead, okay?

527
00:29:53,690 --> 00:29:57,103
- Be careful.
- Careful, careful.

528
00:29:57,103 --> 00:29:58,611
- Evacuate.
- Evacuate?

529
00:29:58,611 --> 00:29:59,727
- Oh, my.
- Why?

530
00:29:59,727 --> 00:30:02,892
It's obvious. Mom's giving
her daughter-in-law a hard time again.

531
00:30:04,551 --> 00:30:07,259
What's it this time?
What's she unhappy about now?

532
00:30:07,259 --> 00:30:10,726
Tae Seong got caught
doing the dishes in the kitchen.

533
00:30:10,726 --> 00:30:11,726
Oh, my.

534
00:30:11,726 --> 00:30:12,799
What?

535
00:30:12,799 --> 00:30:14,859
Take that off. Take it off.

536
00:30:14,859 --> 00:30:16,192
- I said take it off!
- Oh, I'm done.

537
00:30:16,192 --> 00:30:18,355
Take it off, got it?

538
00:30:18,355 --> 00:30:20,755
Did I raise you like that?

539
00:30:20,755 --> 00:30:24,063
I raised you without ever
making you lift a finger.

540
00:30:24,063 --> 00:30:26,126
I'm sorry, Mother.

541
00:30:26,126 --> 00:30:28,071
- I...
- Mom.

542
00:30:28,071 --> 00:30:30,344
She's been working all day.
I just told her to rest a bit.

543
00:30:30,344 --> 00:30:33,263
How much work could she possibly have done?

544
00:30:33,263 --> 00:30:35,891
Hey, come out. You, come here!

545
00:30:35,891 --> 00:30:40,692
Do you usually make
our Tae Seong do housework?

546
00:30:42,639 --> 00:30:46,987
No, what housework? I do housework?

547
00:30:46,987 --> 00:30:49,592
Bossing him around. You made him.

548
00:30:49,592 --> 00:30:51,031
No wonder.

549
00:30:51,031 --> 00:30:54,087
You looked way too practiced
for this to be your first time.

550
00:30:54,087 --> 00:30:57,547
Last time, too, when she was away
using work as an excuse,

551
00:30:57,547 --> 00:30:59,479
you cooked and cleaned up after her.

552
00:30:59,479 --> 00:31:01,792
I didn't say anything then,
but I was furious.

553
00:31:01,792 --> 00:31:03,859
- Mom! That was me...
- Mom, we're here.

554
00:31:03,859 --> 00:31:05,426
We brought kimchi.

555
00:31:05,426 --> 00:31:06,426
- You're here?
- Guys.

556
00:31:06,426 --> 00:31:08,439
You had a hard time, right?

557
00:31:08,439 --> 00:31:11,492
Good grief, Tae Seong is doing the dishes.

558
00:31:11,492 --> 00:31:14,431
He never once set foot in the kitchen.

559
00:31:14,431 --> 00:31:17,187
Imagine how much pressure
she must've put on him.

560
00:31:17,187 --> 00:31:19,583
Goodness, what on earth is going on?

561
00:31:19,583 --> 00:31:21,127
Mom, she hurt her hand.

562
00:31:21,127 --> 00:31:23,799
How did her perfectly fine hand
suddenly get hurt?

563
00:31:23,799 --> 00:31:24,892
She's faking it
because she doesn't want to work.

564
00:31:24,892 --> 00:31:26,599
You're hurt?

565
00:31:26,599 --> 00:31:28,459
- No, I'm fine.
- You should've been more careful.

566
00:31:28,459 --> 00:31:30,583
- Just a little. This tiny bit.
- Oh, dear.

567
00:31:30,583 --> 00:31:32,726
- Are you okay?
- Now that we're all gathered.

568
00:31:34,295 --> 00:31:37,879
Let's settle this once and for all.

569
00:31:37,879 --> 00:31:40,271
- What?
- Here's what I think.

570
00:31:40,271 --> 00:31:42,527
Settle what?
Honey, what are you talking about?

571
00:31:42,527 --> 00:31:44,563
- Don't do this.
- I think that...

572
00:31:44,563 --> 00:31:45,693
it's our family's ancestral rite,

573
00:31:45,693 --> 00:31:47,267
yet you're making
the daughter-in-law do all the work?

574
00:31:47,267 --> 00:31:49,651
I think this is unfair.

575
00:31:49,651 --> 00:31:53,326
Times have changed,
so men should help out too.

576
00:31:53,326 --> 00:31:55,119
And she's going back to work now too.

577
00:31:55,119 --> 00:31:58,691
So, from now on, I'll come early
and help out more. Okay?

578
00:31:58,691 --> 00:32:00,819
- No.
- What a load of nonsense.

579
00:32:00,819 --> 00:32:02,511
Who says anyone's doing anything?

580
00:32:02,511 --> 00:32:03,635
Jeez.

581
00:32:03,635 --> 00:32:08,411
Why are you suddenly acting like this
when you've always listened to Mom?

582
00:32:08,411 --> 00:32:10,128
And from now on,
you should come early and help too.

583
00:32:10,128 --> 00:32:13,003
Don't leave it all to Bo Na.

584
00:32:13,003 --> 00:32:15,326
Kwon Tae Seong, you're being ridiculous.

585
00:32:15,326 --> 00:32:17,755
Sun Il, that's not what he...

586
00:32:17,755 --> 00:32:18,755
Oh, I'm sorry.

587
00:32:18,755 --> 00:32:21,407
It's fine when Mom and your sisters
work themselves to death,

588
00:32:21,407 --> 00:32:24,859
but you can't stand
seeing your wife struggle?

589
00:32:24,859 --> 00:32:27,659
- That's not what I meant...
- Oh, both of you, stop it.

590
00:32:27,659 --> 00:32:29,935
Tae Seong isn't wrong about a single thing.

591
00:32:29,935 --> 00:32:32,826
He finally came to his senses. Good for him.

592
00:32:32,826 --> 00:32:35,483
The timing is just annoying.

593
00:32:35,483 --> 00:32:37,985
He acted like he didn't know all this time,
but why is he doing this now?

594
00:32:37,985 --> 00:32:41,759
What do you think?
It's all because his wife put him up to it.

595
00:32:41,759 --> 00:32:44,726
Oh, my poor son.
What am I going to do with my son now?

596
00:32:44,726 --> 00:32:47,019
Oh, Mom, enough with the "my son" routine.

597
00:32:47,019 --> 00:32:51,581
These days, it's not normal for one woman
to shoulder all the housework alone.

598
00:32:51,581 --> 00:32:54,724
While we're at it, let's get rid of
this outdated ancestral rite too, yeah?

599
00:32:54,724 --> 00:32:55,898
Huh?

600
00:32:55,898 --> 00:32:57,282
Shut your mouth, you girl!

601
00:32:57,282 --> 00:32:58,959
Stay out of it.

602
00:32:58,959 --> 00:33:02,352
Hey, if you have a mouth, say something.

603
00:33:02,352 --> 00:33:04,415
Is that how your parents raised you?

604
00:33:04,415 --> 00:33:06,259
- Mom!
- Mom!

605
00:33:17,459 --> 00:33:21,127
Honey, put on your coat. Let's go home.

606
00:33:29,719 --> 00:33:32,307
Yul, be careful not to get hurt.

607
00:33:32,307 --> 00:33:34,007
Okay.

608
00:33:36,035 --> 00:33:39,619
Kwon Se Ah, who never cared
what anyone thought,

609
00:33:39,619 --> 00:33:41,719
is actually worried about what a kid thinks.

610
00:33:41,719 --> 00:33:44,392
Parenting is hard, indeed.

611
00:33:46,433 --> 00:33:48,439
I wonder if she's finally calmed down.

612
00:33:48,439 --> 00:33:50,585
What did you just say?

613
00:33:50,585 --> 00:33:51,692
We're not participating
in the ancestral rites anymore.

614
00:33:51,692 --> 00:33:53,915
What are you doing? I said put on your coat.

615
00:33:53,915 --> 00:33:55,811
What are you saying you won't do?

616
00:33:55,811 --> 00:33:57,426
- Oh, my.
- Mother!

617
00:33:57,426 --> 00:33:59,159
Mom, Mom...

618
00:34:00,575 --> 00:34:03,355
I think I was being short-sighted.

619
00:34:03,355 --> 00:34:06,299
I used to think
going along with everything you said

620
00:34:06,299 --> 00:34:10,267
was the best way to keep the peace,
but not anymore.

621
00:34:10,267 --> 00:34:16,103
Just as I'm your precious son,
she's my precious wife.

622
00:34:16,103 --> 00:34:19,823
Mom, I'm so scared that one day
she might suddenly disappear from my side.

623
00:34:19,823 --> 00:34:23,455
Just imagining it makes me
feel like I can't breathe.

624
00:34:23,455 --> 00:34:25,103
She is my precious family.

625
00:34:25,103 --> 00:34:29,426
So please, don't ever treat my wife
or my family that way again.

626
00:34:31,592 --> 00:34:35,692
- Unbelievable, that... that punk...
- Mom, Mom!

627
00:34:42,215 --> 00:34:43,915
This...

628
00:34:45,771 --> 00:34:47,626
Why am I...

629
00:34:50,315 --> 00:34:52,159
How did I...

630
00:34:53,443 --> 00:34:55,326
Mother, I'm sorry.

631
00:34:55,326 --> 00:34:57,626
I'm sorry. I shouldn't be receiving this...

632
00:34:59,811 --> 00:35:02,683
Wait... Hey, Kwon Tae Seong!

633
00:35:02,683 --> 00:35:04,392
Aren't you coming here?

634
00:35:04,392 --> 00:35:05,826
- Mom.
- Aren't you coming here?

635
00:35:05,826 --> 00:35:07,592
What are you really trying to do?

636
00:35:07,592 --> 00:35:09,426
- Apologize to your mom.
- What's wrong with you?

637
00:35:09,426 --> 00:35:10,526
And why are you acting like this too?

638
00:35:10,526 --> 00:35:11,726
You're just going to leave after this?

639
00:35:11,726 --> 00:35:13,059
Why are you picking up the dried pollock?

640
00:35:13,059 --> 00:35:14,392
You're just going to leave like this?

641
00:35:14,392 --> 00:35:16,823
- Hurry up and say you're sorry.
- You have no manners.

642
00:35:16,823 --> 00:35:18,179
Oh, stop.

643
00:35:18,179 --> 00:35:19,859
- Stop it!
- You dare?

644
00:35:19,859 --> 00:35:20,999
- You little punk!
- Mom?

645
00:35:20,999 --> 00:35:22,783
- Mom!
- Oh, my!

646
00:35:22,783 --> 00:35:23,792
Are you okay?

647
00:35:23,792 --> 00:35:24,992
You little...

648
00:35:24,992 --> 00:35:26,159
Stop it! No!

649
00:35:26,159 --> 00:35:27,959
You little punk!

650
00:35:29,931 --> 00:35:31,395
You little punk!

651
00:35:31,395 --> 00:35:32,615
Seriously, you...

652
00:35:32,615 --> 00:35:33,692
Hey, come here!

653
00:35:33,692 --> 00:35:34,726
[Pancake Mix]
Come here.

654
00:35:34,726 --> 00:35:36,331
You little punk!

655
00:35:36,331 --> 00:35:39,126
How dare you do this here?

656
00:35:58,459 --> 00:36:02,359
Well, I guess she's
the only person in the world

657
00:36:02,359 --> 00:36:03,679
who can actually chew Yoo Bo Na out.

658
00:36:03,679 --> 00:36:07,059
There's always something new
to learn and master.

659
00:36:07,059 --> 00:36:08,895
That's what running a household is like.

660
00:36:08,895 --> 00:36:11,492
You just have to break through
them again. What can you do?

661
00:36:11,492 --> 00:36:13,607
Just grind it out with sheer effort.

662
00:36:13,607 --> 00:36:17,326
Well, sometimes no amount of effort
can get you through something.

663
00:36:17,326 --> 00:36:21,292
Jeez, that old lady really never changes.

664
00:36:21,292 --> 00:36:24,399
It's about time she showed a bit of mercy.

665
00:36:24,399 --> 00:36:26,731
Will it get better as more time passes?

666
00:36:26,731 --> 00:36:30,959
Yeah, after all that rubbing
each other the wrong way,

667
00:36:31,588 --> 00:36:36,815
laughing and crying together,
physically clashing and hurting each other,

668
00:36:36,815 --> 00:36:39,771
time piles up until it becomes
that thick, sticky bond

669
00:36:39,771 --> 00:36:42,426
we call family.

670
00:36:45,091 --> 00:36:47,126
I guess that's why it's so hard.

671
00:36:49,608 --> 00:36:53,279
Sometimes I find it fascinating,
and sometimes I'm jealous.

672
00:36:53,279 --> 00:36:56,959
Because I've never had anything like that.

673
00:36:58,881 --> 00:37:01,819
Mom! Tae Seong!

674
00:37:01,819 --> 00:37:02,819
Tae Seong!

675
00:37:02,819 --> 00:37:06,292
Yul! Yul is missing!

676
00:37:07,999 --> 00:37:09,699
Bo Na...

677
00:37:10,807 --> 00:37:12,107
Yul!

678
00:37:12,107 --> 00:37:13,671
- Yul!
- Yul...

679
00:37:13,671 --> 00:37:15,623
- You look for her too! Hurry!
- Mom.

680
00:37:15,623 --> 00:37:16,623
Oh, she's not here.

681
00:37:16,623 --> 00:37:18,747
- Yul!
- Is she not there?

682
00:37:18,747 --> 00:37:19,975
- She's not there?
- No.

683
00:37:19,975 --> 00:37:22,247
- What do I do?
- Go check over there.

684
00:37:22,247 --> 00:37:24,059
Yul!

685
00:37:24,059 --> 00:37:25,891
Here? Was she here?

686
00:37:25,891 --> 00:37:27,559
Kwon Se Ah, are you sure you lost her here?

687
00:37:27,559 --> 00:37:33,342
Yeah! I was... I was sitting right here,
and Yul was playing over there.

688
00:37:33,342 --> 00:37:36,559
Chiba! Chiba's leash
came loose, and it ran off,

689
00:37:36,559 --> 00:37:41,126
so I went after it and came back,
but Yul was gone.

690
00:37:41,126 --> 00:37:43,326
Oh, seriously, this kid...

691
00:37:43,326 --> 00:37:44,831
- Yul!
- Oh, for goodness' sake.

692
00:37:44,831 --> 00:37:47,611
Come on, stop crying, you girl.
It's driving me crazy, seriously.

693
00:37:47,611 --> 00:37:50,063
Hey, you take her
and go back inside the house.

694
00:37:50,063 --> 00:37:53,243
Clean up the mess in there.

695
00:37:53,243 --> 00:37:56,226
Mom, is that really what you say
to a mom who's just lost her child?

696
00:37:57,251 --> 00:37:59,715
Yeah, okay. Got it, Tae Seong.

697
00:37:59,715 --> 00:38:03,875
Yeah, when he gets there,
check the CCTV and call me.

698
00:38:03,875 --> 00:38:06,115
It's Tae Seong. He couldn't reach
the security guard earlier,

699
00:38:06,115 --> 00:38:07,995
but he just got through,
and the guard is on his way.

700
00:38:07,995 --> 00:38:11,439
Let's split up and search
the area for now, okay?

701
00:38:11,439 --> 00:38:12,639
Split up. Go.

702
00:38:12,639 --> 00:38:14,315
You go that way. I'll check over there.

703
00:38:14,315 --> 00:38:16,159
That way...

704
00:38:23,219 --> 00:38:24,355
Ms. Yoo!

705
00:38:24,355 --> 00:38:25,611
Oh, Assistant Manager Ki!

706
00:38:25,611 --> 00:38:27,367
You got here sooner than I expected.

707
00:38:27,367 --> 00:38:28,695
Thank you so much for coming.

708
00:38:28,695 --> 00:38:30,279
You said you lost a child, so...

709
00:38:30,279 --> 00:38:32,426
What do I do?

710
00:38:32,426 --> 00:38:33,991
- This...
- That one?

711
00:38:33,991 --> 00:38:37,195
Yeah, can you do it? Is it possible?

712
00:38:37,195 --> 00:38:40,815
So this is what it means
to feel chills and get goosebumps.

713
00:38:40,815 --> 00:38:42,659
I'm counting on you.

714
00:38:43,487 --> 00:38:45,394
Where on earth is she?

715
00:38:45,394 --> 00:38:47,526
Jeez, I'm going crazy.

716
00:38:49,303 --> 00:38:51,392
Oh, Bo Na...

717
00:38:56,315 --> 00:38:57,415
- Se Ah.
- Bo Na.

718
00:38:57,415 --> 00:38:58,887
Se Ah, what's the situation?

719
00:38:58,887 --> 00:39:00,263
Did you check Seo Yeon's place?

720
00:39:00,263 --> 00:39:02,059
Well, they said she never came there either.

721
00:39:02,059 --> 00:39:05,949
And... I didn't see her on the way here.

722
00:39:05,949 --> 00:39:10,592
I'm so sorry, Bo Na.
I should've been watching her better.

723
00:39:12,291 --> 00:39:13,492
We'll find her.

724
00:39:13,492 --> 00:39:16,151
Yul is a smart girl. She'll be okay.

725
00:39:16,151 --> 00:39:17,851
It's okay.

726
00:39:23,155 --> 00:39:26,399
But who is that?

727
00:39:26,399 --> 00:39:30,059
Oh, he's a coworker of mine.

728
00:39:30,059 --> 00:39:31,259
Hacking is his hobby,

729
00:39:31,259 --> 00:39:34,892
so I asked him to see if he could
access those CCTV cameras.

730
00:39:34,892 --> 00:39:38,160
And you know this
has to stay a secret, right?

731
00:39:38,160 --> 00:39:42,435
Yes, I've never met a hacker
in real life before.

732
00:39:42,435 --> 00:39:43,603
It's done.

733
00:39:43,603 --> 00:39:45,792
Huh?

734
00:39:48,255 --> 00:39:50,395
What's the exact time the child went missing?

735
00:39:50,395 --> 00:39:54,126
Sometime between 6:30 p.m. and 7 p.m.

736
00:39:56,383 --> 00:39:58,083
I found her.

737
00:40:08,547 --> 00:40:12,792
Luckily, no one took her.
She left on her own.

738
00:40:13,683 --> 00:40:15,383
Thank goodness.

739
00:40:16,431 --> 00:40:18,971
She seems to have wandered
around the apartment complex,

740
00:40:18,971 --> 00:40:24,091
then left the complex
and headed toward the main road.

741
00:40:24,091 --> 00:40:25,411
The main road?

742
00:40:25,411 --> 00:40:28,539
Then I'll check that way.
Let me know if you find anything.

743
00:40:28,539 --> 00:40:30,239
Oh...

744
00:40:35,347 --> 00:40:39,259
Were you the one
who was with her until the end?

745
00:40:41,055 --> 00:40:42,143
Yes.

746
00:40:42,143 --> 00:40:44,287
Do you remember anything?

747
00:40:44,287 --> 00:40:47,704
Anything strange about what she said or did?

748
00:40:47,704 --> 00:40:51,740
Oh, well...

749
00:40:51,740 --> 00:40:53,669
Take your time and think.

750
00:40:53,669 --> 00:40:57,392
Even the smallest thing could be a clue.

751
00:40:59,231 --> 00:41:04,171
Yul was asking me a lot of questions.

752
00:41:04,171 --> 00:41:06,711
Auntie, how do you get to heaven?

753
00:41:06,711 --> 00:41:08,579
Heaven? You have to die to go there.

754
00:41:08,579 --> 00:41:11,691
Die, die!

755
00:41:11,691 --> 00:41:16,200
Oh, no! I must've been crazy!

756
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:20,292
She asked how to get to heaven.

757
00:41:20,292 --> 00:41:23,747
I told her you have to die.

758
00:41:23,747 --> 00:41:25,891
Oh, what do I do?

759
00:41:25,891 --> 00:41:27,392
Why would you say something like that?

760
00:41:27,392 --> 00:41:29,447
Well...

761
00:41:29,447 --> 00:41:33,949
Yul asked me what the ancestral rite is,

762
00:41:33,949 --> 00:41:39,359
and I told her people come down
from heaven to have a meal...

763
00:41:40,867 --> 00:41:42,792
Oh, my...

764
00:41:42,792 --> 00:41:45,975
This is all my fault.

765
00:41:45,975 --> 00:41:49,626
I was stupid enough
to take my eyes off my niece.

766
00:41:50,267 --> 00:41:54,135
Yul, I'm so sorry.

767
00:41:54,135 --> 00:41:57,131
Stop crying. I think I've found a clue.

768
00:41:57,131 --> 00:41:58,292
What?

769
00:41:58,292 --> 00:42:00,308
Yul going missing isn't your fault.

770
00:42:00,308 --> 00:42:03,726
So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.

771
00:42:14,403 --> 00:42:15,479
Tae Seong!

772
00:42:15,479 --> 00:42:17,847
- Honey!
- Where's Yul?

773
00:42:17,847 --> 00:42:21,683
Well... We'll find Yul soon,
so I don't think you need to worry too much.

774
00:42:21,683 --> 00:42:24,459
Yul went toward the main road, right?

775
00:42:25,267 --> 00:42:27,759
How did you know...

776
00:42:27,759 --> 00:42:29,567
[Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do]

777
00:42:29,567 --> 00:42:31,759
Yeah, Assistant Manager Ki,
what did you find?

778
00:42:33,155 --> 00:42:34,855
What?

779
00:42:38,635 --> 00:42:40,443
She was looking up at the sky.

780
00:42:40,443 --> 00:42:42,931
So there must've been something
in the sky, right?

781
00:42:42,931 --> 00:42:45,679
Judging by the slight movement of her head,

782
00:42:45,679 --> 00:42:47,347
I think it might have been an airplane.

783
00:42:47,347 --> 00:42:48,690
Oh? That's right!

784
00:42:48,690 --> 00:42:51,126
Flights to Gimpo fly over our neighborhood.

785
00:42:51,126 --> 00:42:52,943
Yul loves watching planes,

786
00:42:52,943 --> 00:42:56,203
so sometimes I take her up
to Tae Seong's rooftop...

787
00:42:56,203 --> 00:42:57,926
Oh, my!

788
00:43:03,463 --> 00:43:09,359
From what you said, it seems Yul
wanted to go to heaven for some reason.

789
00:43:36,227 --> 00:43:38,459
I'll get the key.

790
00:43:40,071 --> 00:43:41,771
Yeah.

791
00:43:44,626 --> 00:43:47,995
Take me with you!

792
00:43:47,995 --> 00:43:50,435
Take me with you!

793
00:43:50,435 --> 00:43:52,947
Take me with you too.

794
00:43:52,947 --> 00:43:56,271
Take me with you!

795
00:43:56,271 --> 00:43:59,158
Take me with you.

796
00:43:59,158 --> 00:44:04,112
Come here, and take me with you.

797
00:44:04,112 --> 00:44:07,826
I think she thought the airplane
would take her there.

798
00:44:09,699 --> 00:44:13,320
It was left open for waterproofing work
earlier today, but I locked it just now.

799
00:44:13,320 --> 00:44:17,192
Oh, my God. What on earth happened?

800
00:44:25,567 --> 00:44:27,307
Huh?

801
00:44:27,307 --> 00:44:30,759
Who told you to come up here alone? Huh?
Is that what I taught you?

802
00:44:30,759 --> 00:44:32,491
Are you going to wander around
by yourself at night like this?

803
00:44:32,491 --> 00:44:34,383
Why did you come up here
in the middle of the night?

804
00:44:34,383 --> 00:44:37,926
Are you hurt anywhere?
Are you going to do that again?

805
00:44:39,011 --> 00:44:41,651
I was going to bring them back.

806
00:44:41,651 --> 00:44:43,891
Who? Bring who back?

807
00:44:43,891 --> 00:44:46,559
Mommy's mom and dad.

808
00:44:47,423 --> 00:44:51,326
I heard they went to heaven.

809
00:44:53,251 --> 00:44:57,392
I was going to bring them back on a plane.

810
00:44:58,400 --> 00:45:01,619
Because Mommy is an orphan.

811
00:45:01,619 --> 00:45:05,559
I don't want Mommy to be an orphan.

812
00:45:17,595 --> 00:45:20,903
I see. I'm sorry. I...

813
00:45:20,903 --> 00:45:23,711
I didn't know how you felt
and scolded you first. I'm sorry.

814
00:45:23,711 --> 00:45:25,028
Don't cry, Yul. Come here.

815
00:45:25,028 --> 00:45:27,326
I'm sorry. Mommy's sorry.

816
00:45:28,835 --> 00:45:31,226
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have done that.

817
00:46:01,787 --> 00:46:02,979
Are you okay?

818
00:46:02,979 --> 00:46:04,679
Huh?

819
00:46:06,167 --> 00:46:08,255
I'm okay.

820
00:46:08,255 --> 00:46:11,017
Anyway, we found Yul safely.

821
00:46:11,017 --> 00:46:12,763
I'm sorry.

822
00:46:12,763 --> 00:46:16,207
But how could you do that to me?

823
00:46:16,207 --> 00:46:20,483
How could you imagine me
suddenly disappearing one day?

824
00:46:20,483 --> 00:46:22,459
How could you imagine such a thing?

825
00:46:23,283 --> 00:46:24,983
Huh?

826
00:46:26,735 --> 00:46:30,043
When you have something precious,
like an expensive jewel,

827
00:46:30,043 --> 00:46:32,155
you're always afraid of losing it.

828
00:46:32,155 --> 00:46:34,454
That's what you are to me.

829
00:46:34,454 --> 00:46:37,226
You're so precious to me...

830
00:46:38,431 --> 00:46:40,792
that I'm afraid I'll lose you.

831
00:46:52,126 --> 00:46:56,511
I mean, you're not usually like this,
so why today...

832
00:46:56,511 --> 00:46:58,383
I don't know. You're in big trouble now.

833
00:46:58,383 --> 00:47:00,959
You totally lost points with Mother.

834
00:47:02,159 --> 00:47:05,992
Well, I can just earn double the points
I lost with Mom from you.

835
00:47:08,667 --> 00:47:12,027
No, I definitely lost a lot of points today.

836
00:47:12,027 --> 00:47:15,211
Because of me,
the ancestral rites were canceled.

837
00:47:15,211 --> 00:47:18,426
But we all decided that by vote, so whatever.

838
00:47:21,755 --> 00:47:24,699
Our Yul really did something big today.

839
00:47:24,699 --> 00:47:28,959
She even softened Grandma's stubborn heart.

840
00:47:28,959 --> 00:47:31,639
My daughter is better than I.

841
00:47:31,639 --> 00:47:34,392
She even comforted her mommy's heart.

842
00:47:38,347 --> 00:47:41,959
I'm supposed to be the one
comforting my daughter.

843
00:47:42,735 --> 00:47:45,937
She's still so young.

844
00:47:45,937 --> 00:47:49,592
I wish she didn't have to
understand things like that yet.

845
00:48:13,375 --> 00:48:15,075
Oh, dear.

846
00:48:16,103 --> 00:48:19,951
She's a mom too, so she went
completely crazy over her own kid.

847
00:48:19,951 --> 00:48:21,727
But still, that's too much.

848
00:48:21,727 --> 00:48:24,559
Still, how can she glare
at her mother-in-law like that?

849
00:48:26,287 --> 00:48:29,292
Because Mommy is an orphan.

850
00:48:30,300 --> 00:48:33,949
I don't want Mommy to be an orphan.

851
00:48:33,949 --> 00:48:35,963
Is it because she's an orphan?

852
00:48:35,963 --> 00:48:40,226
She does seem especially attached
when it comes to her family.

853
00:48:43,499 --> 00:48:45,292
Looks like...

854
00:48:47,224 --> 00:48:50,051
Bo Na is pretty athletic, huh?

855
00:48:50,051 --> 00:48:52,307
You little punk!

856
00:48:52,307 --> 00:48:54,023
No wonder.

857
00:48:54,023 --> 00:48:56,792
Did she do sports
or something back in school?

858
00:48:59,935 --> 00:49:02,743
But why has she been
spacing out since earlier?

859
00:49:02,743 --> 00:49:05,926
So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.

860
00:49:20,382 --> 00:49:21,563
What?

861
00:49:21,563 --> 00:49:23,263
What's wrong with her?

862
00:49:24,647 --> 00:49:27,459
She must still be shaken up from losing Yul.

863
00:49:29,937 --> 00:49:34,659
Anyway, I'm so relieved the ancestral rites
are over as of today!

864
00:49:35,300 --> 00:49:37,249
What an ungrateful bunch!

865
00:49:37,249 --> 00:49:39,687
You don't care about your mom one bit.

866
00:49:39,687 --> 00:49:42,671
Oh, our dear Ok Seon Ja, what's wrong now?

867
00:49:42,671 --> 00:49:45,192
If there's no ancestral rite,
you're the one who'll have it easiest.

868
00:49:45,192 --> 00:49:47,629
Easy for you to say.

869
00:49:47,629 --> 00:49:49,639
I've done this my whole life.

870
00:49:49,639 --> 00:49:53,716
If we abolish it now,
how am I supposed to face our ancestors?

871
00:49:53,716 --> 00:49:55,911
Oh, Mom!

872
00:49:55,911 --> 00:49:57,547
It's settled.
Why are you bringing it up again?

873
00:49:57,547 --> 00:50:02,263
We voted on whether to abolish it,
and the majority voted yes.

874
00:50:02,263 --> 00:50:04,359
That's it! Done! Over!

875
00:50:05,286 --> 00:50:09,199
Let's go clean up that mess over there.

876
00:50:09,199 --> 00:50:12,392
Oh, my, when are we ever
going to clean all that up?

877
00:50:13,167 --> 00:50:14,541
You godless bunch!

878
00:50:14,541 --> 00:50:18,759
Just you wait!
I'll do it all by myself next year.

879
00:50:29,939 --> 00:50:32,715
By the way, what was the vote count?

880
00:50:32,715 --> 00:50:34,191
- Huh?
- You counted the votes.

881
00:50:34,191 --> 00:50:36,435
You're the only one who saw the results.

882
00:50:36,435 --> 00:50:39,659
Well, obviously,
Mom was the one vote against it.

883
00:50:41,671 --> 00:50:43,626
That's...

884
00:50:53,727 --> 00:50:55,711
a secret.

885
00:50:55,711 --> 00:50:57,187
Why?

886
00:50:57,187 --> 00:50:58,959
Tell me, please.

887
00:50:58,959 --> 00:51:02,562
We agreed to keep the vote count secret.

888
00:51:02,562 --> 00:51:04,559
But tell me.

889
00:51:04,559 --> 00:51:07,009
Fine, I'm going to sulk.

890
00:51:07,009 --> 00:51:08,451
What's wrong?

891
00:51:08,451 --> 00:51:10,667
Please don't talk to me.

892
00:51:10,667 --> 00:51:14,259
And I don't think I'll get over this easily.

893
00:51:16,347 --> 00:51:19,571
Please tell me! Please!

894
00:51:19,571 --> 00:51:21,226
- Are you really that curious?
- Yeah.

895
00:51:21,226 --> 00:51:23,026
I guess you would be.

896
00:51:23,026 --> 00:51:25,326
Come on, really?

897
00:51:32,783 --> 00:51:34,892
Help me!

898
00:51:34,892 --> 00:51:37,192
Help me! Please, over here!

899
00:51:37,192 --> 00:51:38,926
I'm falling! Help me!

900
00:51:38,926 --> 00:51:40,626
Help me!

901
00:51:40,626 --> 00:51:43,126
Help me! Please!

902
00:51:54,612 --> 00:51:57,643
We've determined that Tak Jong Gu
spends his time going back and forth

903
00:51:57,643 --> 00:52:02,483
between the 22nd-floor VIP gaming room
and the 23rd-floor VIP suite.

904
00:52:02,483 --> 00:52:06,947
His dad has forbidden him from leaving,
so he can't go outside

905
00:52:06,947 --> 00:52:09,495
and takes care of everything
inside this building.

906
00:52:09,495 --> 00:52:12,674
And since the gaming room is a sealed,
windowless space,

907
00:52:12,674 --> 00:52:15,279
he can't be sniped from outside.

908
00:52:15,279 --> 00:52:19,039
So that means we'd have to target him
while he's inside his suite.

909
00:52:19,039 --> 00:52:20,739
The problem is that...

910
00:52:21,931 --> 00:52:26,371
Tak Jong Gu's room, 2305,
is on this side of the building.

911
00:52:26,371 --> 00:52:29,427
As you can see, the front window
has a completely open view.

912
00:52:29,427 --> 00:52:33,526
And the convention center next door
is almost directly opposite it.

913
00:52:34,175 --> 00:52:37,300
So there's no angle for a sniper shot.

914
00:52:37,300 --> 00:52:41,692
Then we'd have to lure him outside first.

915
00:52:41,692 --> 00:52:45,861
So the only way for us to get close is
through the 22nd-floor gaming room?

916
00:52:45,861 --> 00:52:47,987
The 22nd-floor gaming room is for VIPs only,

917
00:52:47,987 --> 00:52:50,583
so ordinary guests can't access it.

918
00:52:50,583 --> 00:52:55,292
There is, however, one way
for ordinary guests to get in.

919
00:52:56,159 --> 00:52:57,855
Every day, the person

920
00:52:57,855 --> 00:53:01,427
who wins the most chips
in the first-floor public gaming room

921
00:53:01,427 --> 00:53:03,448
gets a pass to the VIP gaming room.

922
00:53:03,448 --> 00:53:06,326
It's basically a one-day pass.

923
00:53:08,474 --> 00:53:11,651
So they expect you to win downstairs
and lose it all upstairs.

924
00:53:11,651 --> 00:53:14,587
We're barely covering
operating expenses this month.

925
00:53:14,587 --> 00:53:17,549
So, one of us just needs to
pose as a customer

926
00:53:17,549 --> 00:53:22,074
and to win that VIP pass.

927
00:53:22,074 --> 00:53:25,707
Tak Jong Gu mainly plays blackjack.

928
00:53:25,707 --> 00:53:27,992
Anyone here know how to play blackjack?

929
00:53:29,078 --> 00:53:30,527
I've never played blackjack before.

930
00:53:30,527 --> 00:53:31,655
Then what games have you played?

931
00:53:31,655 --> 00:53:32,828
One Card.

932
00:53:32,828 --> 00:53:33,967
One Card?

933
00:53:33,967 --> 00:53:35,235
Is that any fun?

934
00:53:35,235 --> 00:53:36,935
No one?

935
00:53:40,503 --> 00:53:44,226
Has anyone ever won money playing blackjack?

936
00:54:05,881 --> 00:54:10,623
In blackjack, the player whose cards
total 21 or come closest to 21 wins,

937
00:54:10,623 --> 00:54:12,815
giving the dealer and player
roughly equal odds.

938
00:54:12,815 --> 00:54:16,492
So I created a program
that maximizes those odds.

939
00:54:17,636 --> 00:54:20,171
These glasses have the program
built into them.

940
00:54:20,171 --> 00:54:22,295
They recognize the cards that
have been played and those remaining,

941
00:54:22,295 --> 00:54:26,459
and then signal whether I should
hit or stay with lights only I can see.

942
00:54:35,733 --> 00:54:39,039
Congratulations.
This is your pass to the VIP gaming room.

943
00:54:39,039 --> 00:54:40,739
Thank you.

944
00:54:50,799 --> 00:54:54,459
So we'll get the VIP pass
this way, go upstairs,

945
00:54:55,466 --> 00:54:57,173
and approach Tak Jong Gu.

946
00:54:57,173 --> 00:55:00,759
We'll drop a pill into his drink.

947
00:55:01,431 --> 00:55:03,255
It's a drug that causes vasculitis.

948
00:55:03,255 --> 00:55:07,863
A few minutes after he takes it,
red spots will break out all over his body.

949
00:55:07,863 --> 00:55:09,547
Get a doctor now!

950
00:55:09,547 --> 00:55:11,939
Get the doctor!

951
00:55:11,939 --> 00:55:15,403
That's when Manager Go will appear
disguised as the on-site doctor.

952
00:55:15,403 --> 00:55:17,515
Hey! What's this?

953
00:55:17,515 --> 00:55:18,903
It's an acute allergic reaction.

954
00:55:18,903 --> 00:55:20,771
You could go into shock
if we leave you like this.

955
00:55:20,771 --> 00:55:22,859
We need to get you to a hospital right away.

956
00:55:26,867 --> 00:55:29,326
Once we get Tak Jong Gu outside, we're done.

957
00:55:51,226 --> 00:55:54,491
[Hongseon Rest Area]

958
00:55:54,491 --> 00:55:56,619
He didn't fall while working,

959
00:55:56,619 --> 00:55:59,899
so why was he there in the middle
of the night, and how did he fall?

960
00:55:59,899 --> 00:56:03,199
And from the exact same spot
where Kang Yeong Ho fell to his death.

961
00:56:03,199 --> 00:56:05,395
What does the police say?

962
00:56:05,395 --> 00:56:07,203
Looks like they don't have
any answers either.

963
00:56:07,203 --> 00:56:10,031
It was late at night in a remote area,
so there were no witnesses.

964
00:56:10,031 --> 00:56:12,335
Wow, but that Park Chun Bok guy,

965
00:56:12,335 --> 00:56:14,963
he acted like such a saint
during the interview.

966
00:56:14,963 --> 00:56:16,841
But he had assault, theft,
and even attempted murder on his record.

967
00:56:16,841 --> 00:56:19,839
A whopping five-time ex-con!

968
00:56:19,839 --> 00:56:22,831
You really can't judge a person
by appearances.

969
00:56:22,831 --> 00:56:27,599
And before he died, he was handing out money
from some unknown source?

970
00:56:27,599 --> 00:56:31,228
This feels like a terrifying case
involving Chairman Cheon Seong Gil,

971
00:56:31,228 --> 00:56:32,551
the field workers, and everyone in between.

972
00:56:32,551 --> 00:56:35,947
It seems like a complex and terrifying case.

973
00:56:35,947 --> 00:56:38,208
Anyway, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
is at the center of it.

974
00:56:38,208 --> 00:56:40,326
Let's go meet him first.

975
00:56:41,579 --> 00:56:44,423
Do you think he'll see us?
He already refused our interview.

976
00:56:44,423 --> 00:56:46,679
Who says we have to do a formal interview?

977
00:56:46,679 --> 00:56:48,379
Oh!

978
00:56:55,639 --> 00:56:57,383
Seven.

979
00:56:57,383 --> 00:56:59,578
Hit.

980
00:56:59,578 --> 00:57:01,292
Thirteen.

981
00:57:05,393 --> 00:57:07,126
Stay.

982
00:57:08,139 --> 00:57:09,211
Fourteen.

983
00:57:09,211 --> 00:57:11,259
Twenty-four, bust.

984
00:57:17,339 --> 00:57:19,039
Eighteen.

985
00:57:20,159 --> 00:57:21,859
Stay.

986
00:57:35,803 --> 00:57:37,526
Eleven.

987
00:57:39,471 --> 00:57:41,491
- Down.
- Double down.

988
00:57:41,491 --> 00:57:43,399
[Double Down: Double your bet
and get one more card]

989
00:57:44,965 --> 00:57:46,559
Twenty-three. Dealer bust.

990
00:57:46,559 --> 00:57:48,471
[Bust: The total exceeds 21]

991
00:57:48,471 --> 00:57:50,408
Twenty-one.

992
00:57:50,408 --> 00:57:53,759
Congratulations. Your double down paid off.

993
00:57:56,149 --> 00:57:57,623
- Nice, blackjack!
- Blackjack!

994
00:57:57,623 --> 00:57:59,011
Congratulations!

995
00:57:59,011 --> 00:58:00,692
Would you like to take even money?

996
00:58:00,692 --> 00:58:01,927
[Even Money: If the dealer
might also have blackjack,]

997
00:58:01,927 --> 00:58:03,167
[you give up the 1.5:1 payout
and take 1:1 instead. A kind of insurance]

998
00:58:03,167 --> 00:58:04,923
Sure.

999
00:58:04,923 --> 00:58:07,351
Oh, come on.

1000
00:58:07,351 --> 00:58:09,626
Don't do that.

1001
00:58:10,943 --> 00:58:13,671
You've got to go for it here,
even if you might lose.

1002
00:58:13,671 --> 00:58:16,459
Are you new to gambling?

1003
00:58:21,835 --> 00:58:23,495
Eighteen.

1004
00:58:23,495 --> 00:58:25,992
See? You barely won anything.

1005
00:58:25,992 --> 00:58:29,259
Making pennies like that,
when are you ever going to get rich?

1006
00:58:31,959 --> 00:58:35,478
Still, that's a decent win
for someone so chicken-hearted, huh?

1007
00:58:35,478 --> 00:58:38,259
Would you like to join the game, ma'am?

1008
00:58:39,183 --> 00:58:41,266
Me?

1009
00:58:41,266 --> 00:58:43,629
Oh, jeez.

1010
00:58:43,629 --> 00:58:46,659
I really shouldn't do this.

1011
00:58:47,911 --> 00:58:51,492
I really quit gambling.

1012
00:58:59,559 --> 00:59:01,392
[Gaecheon Construction]

1013
00:59:04,955 --> 00:59:09,359
Huh? Isn't that Chairman Cheon's car?

1014
00:59:21,623 --> 00:59:24,359
Looks like he's going somewhere.
What do we do?

1015
00:59:25,571 --> 00:59:28,783
What do you mean? We have to follow him.

1016
00:59:28,783 --> 00:59:30,492
Again?

1017
00:59:35,403 --> 00:59:36,459
Seventeen.

1018
00:59:36,459 --> 00:59:38,008
- Yes!
- Wow!

1019
00:59:38,008 --> 00:59:40,126
How many wins is that?

1020
00:59:48,239 --> 00:59:51,098
It's been so long
since I've felt this thrill.

1021
00:59:51,098 --> 00:59:54,659
Okay, from now on,

1022
00:59:54,659 --> 00:59:56,899
[Three Hands: One person plays three hands]
should I go three hands?

1023
00:59:56,899 --> 00:59:59,749
- Join?
- I'm good.

1024
00:59:59,749 --> 01:00:01,247
Chicken.

1025
01:00:01,247 --> 01:00:03,526
[Pair: First two cards have the same value]
I'm betting on a pair too.

1026
01:00:04,739 --> 01:00:06,526
No more bets?

1027
01:00:15,059 --> 01:00:17,083
Nice pair.

1028
01:00:17,083 --> 01:00:18,783
Yes!

1029
01:00:20,907 --> 01:00:23,149
Yeah.

1030
01:00:23,149 --> 01:00:24,219
Congratulations!

1031
01:00:24,219 --> 01:00:26,931
This is a pass granting
you access to the VIP gaming room.

1032
01:00:26,931 --> 01:00:29,891
Wow, thank you!

1033
01:00:29,891 --> 01:00:32,512
Thank you! Thank you!

1034
01:00:32,512 --> 01:00:34,259
Thank you!

1035
01:00:41,569 --> 01:00:43,507
Good job, chicken.

1036
01:00:43,507 --> 01:00:45,547
You should quit while you're ahead.

1037
01:00:45,547 --> 01:00:48,392
You'll lose everything otherwise.

1038
01:00:52,095 --> 01:00:53,187
See you around!

1039
01:00:59,291 --> 01:01:01,586
Oh, I lost!

1040
01:01:01,586 --> 01:01:04,024
I lost again!

1041
01:01:04,024 --> 01:01:06,663
Mister, I lost again.

1042
01:01:06,663 --> 01:01:09,759
I lost again!

1043
01:01:11,679 --> 01:01:13,379
What are you doing here again?

1044
01:01:16,124 --> 01:01:18,199
Even your plans fail sometimes.

1045
01:01:18,199 --> 01:01:20,259
I'm sorry, Ms. Yoo.

1046
01:01:23,600 --> 01:01:27,387
But there are always
unexpected variables in the field.

1047
01:01:27,387 --> 01:01:31,396
And cleaning up after a junior's mistakes
is part of being a good senior.

1048
01:01:31,396 --> 01:01:33,692
What are you thinking?

1049
01:01:33,692 --> 01:01:34,935
I'm thinking maybe I should go in directly.

1050
01:01:34,935 --> 01:01:37,027
You, personally?

1051
01:01:37,027 --> 01:01:38,199
The gaming room might be difficult,

1052
01:01:38,199 --> 01:01:40,735
but wouldn't it be easier
to sneak into his suite?

1053
01:01:40,735 --> 01:01:42,923
I'll just drug his water and get out.

1054
01:01:42,923 --> 01:01:45,163
That's our best option right now.

1055
01:01:45,163 --> 01:01:46,587
I can't agree to that.

1056
01:01:46,587 --> 01:01:48,592
It's too dangerous for you
to expose yourself on-site.

1057
01:01:48,592 --> 01:01:51,455
You will back me up, won't you?

1058
01:01:51,455 --> 01:01:52,671
- Well, that's...
- Tell Manager Go

1059
01:01:52,671 --> 01:01:55,526
about the revised plan beforehand.

1060
01:01:57,267 --> 01:01:59,647
Okay, shall we go?

1061
01:01:59,647 --> 01:02:01,347
Ms. Yoo.

1062
01:02:02,331 --> 01:02:05,326
You know your safety comes first, right?

1063
01:02:12,719 --> 01:02:14,226
No, wait a moment.

1064
01:02:14,226 --> 01:02:15,574
Chairman!

1065
01:02:15,574 --> 01:02:19,926
Please, just let me in for a moment!

1066
01:02:19,926 --> 01:02:21,187
Oh, please!

1067
01:02:21,187 --> 01:02:23,159
Just a moment.

1068
01:03:10,783 --> 01:03:11,967
How bad is this guy?

1069
01:03:11,967 --> 01:03:14,359
On the surface,
it looks like an accidental mishap,

1070
01:03:14,359 --> 01:03:16,087
but a premeditated murder underneath?

1071
01:03:16,087 --> 01:03:18,385
- Done.
- Someone's coming down the hall.

1072
01:03:18,385 --> 01:03:19,395
A reporter?

1073
01:03:19,395 --> 01:03:21,815
Well, this just got interesting.

1074
01:03:21,815 --> 01:03:24,207
No, it's too dangerous for you
to meet him there yourself.

1075
01:03:24,207 --> 01:03:25,937
That woman could become a witness...

1076
01:03:25,937 --> 01:03:27,466
What's the variable this time?

1077
01:03:27,466 --> 01:03:28,816
Someone else is coming down the hall.

1078
01:03:28,816 --> 01:03:30,859
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo!

1079
01:03:30,859 --> 01:03:33,831
In the end, the day will come
when that secret is revealed.

1080
01:03:33,831 --> 01:03:36,024
It's all my fault.

1081
01:03:36,024 --> 01:03:39,526
Calm down. Director Yoo will be fine.

1082
01:03:40,143 --> 01:03:41,279
What's wrong?

1083
01:03:41,279 --> 01:03:43,259
It's someone I know.

1084
01:03:45,483 --> 01:03:47,483
MkvDrama.Net
